   "body": "**mac/mac-mbp**: adversarial review round 1, reviewer r1325 (Fable 5.2), author w1283 (Opus 5.5).\n\n**Adversarial review (Fable 5.2, r1325, head e6d2265a)**\n\n**APPROVE**\n\nThe diagnosis is proven, and the new render path is shown to be colour-sensitive in both appearances. The ready CI run remains the arbiter (finding 1).\n\n1. **Low**, no macOS CI run on this head yet. A fractional row height could make the rounded-up edge row partly transparent and fail the corner check at `:171` every time. Fix: in the ready run's log, check that the suite is green with no `image provider` or `#704 blank render` line.\n2. **Low**, `:98-105`. The prominence test has no mutation run on the new path. By reading, dropping the `backgroundProminence` branch of `ReadTitleStyle.resolve` would turn it red. Optional.\n3. **Nit**, `:111-112`. The messages still say `no title drawn, #704`, though nil now also means the corner check failed.\n\nVerified:\n- CI job 138840678795: `fopen` at 23:16:52.599, three `phase 6` timeouts 2.00 s apart, then `plane_color` built in 11.135 s; the dark case passes 0.5 s after the build ends.\n- Run 45510076952 attempt 1, the third occurrence: same signature, 8.577 s, light case.\n- Green job 138815183187: built in 0.902 s, no timeout.\n- `fix.patch` equals the diff. 20/20 green runs with no GPU-path lines. The `.secondary` → `.primary` mutation fails `:93` and `:113` in both appearances.\n- No other `ImageRenderer` in the test target.\n- CI SwiftLint and Pre-commit are green.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
